basically operators are the special symbols which are used to perform operations between and with
variables and values.
there are basically 10 types of operators in js
1. arithemetic = perform basic mathematical calculation on number
2. assignment = assign values to variables oftern combining with arithmetic or bitwise operation
3. comparison = compare two values and return a boolean
4. logical = used with boolean values to combine or invert conditions
5. bitwise = operate directly on the binary representation of numbers
6. string = used to manipulate text
7. unary = work on a single operand 
8. conditional(ternary) = the only ternary operator in js which is shorthand for if..else
9. relational = check relationships between objects and properties
10. comma = allow multiple expressions to be evaluated, returning the last one.
